        "responded_directly": true,
        "direct_response_text": "Canonical Herma + Tessera Noun/Verb Contract -- Tasks (`verbs` on the wire) and Task Objects (`nouns` on the wire: every reusable tool, feed, dataset, LoRA adapter, shim, or receipt a task uses or creates). Shared Task Objects are compare-and-set NOUNs guarded by expected_version, and independently schedulable Tasks are leased VERB tiles (enqueue -> claim -> heartbeat -> submit/park) guarded by a monotonic fence token.\n\n[NOUN/VERB CONTEXT]\n- [NOUN] noun:tessera.lease_fence (Tessera Monotonic Lease Fence): Compare-and-set task lease token incremented on every claim to fence out stale workers. -- {\"fields\":{\"fence\":\"integer >= 1\",\"lease_expires_at\":\"float\",\"task_id\":\"string\"},\"invariant\":\"submit/heartbeat/park reject fence < current_fence\"} [URI: https://tessera.ta-amps.workers.dev/llms.txt]\n- [VERB] verb:tessera.claim (Tessera Atomic Claim Verb): Atomically leases the next highest-priority ready task in a queue and mints a fresh fence token. -- {\"endpoint\":\"POST /v1/queues/{queue}/claim\",\"inputs\":[\"worker_id\",\"lease_seconds\"],\"returns\":[\"task_id\",\"fence\",\"payload\"]} [URI: mcp://tessera/tools/claim]\n[/NOUN/VERB CONTEXT]",
